; Continue only if the command is really being performed
;
; Called just before a command changes the world. When the perform flag
; (#R$B6FA) is 1 it returns; otherwise the command is only being tried: it sets
; the "possible" flag (#R$B6FB) to the perform flag plus one and abandons the
; routine that called it (POP BC drops its return address, so the RET goes to
; that routine's caller).
;
; O:A Perform flag (when it returns)
@label=CommitOrAbort
c$9D44 LD A,($B6FA)
 $9D47 CP $01
 $9D49 RET Z
 $9D4A INC A
 $9D4B LD ($B6FB),A
 $9D4E POP BC           ; drop the return address: leave the caller
 $9D4F RET
